H2.10->supported, H2.10.6->supported, H2.11->supported, H2.11.3->supported, H2.11.5->open, H2.11.6->refuted, H2.18.2->inconclusive, H2.18.3->retired, H2.20.4->refuted, H2.20.5->refuted, H8->open, H8.2->refuted, H8.2.1->refuted, H8.2.2->refuted, H10.1->refuted, H11->open, H11.2->supported, H11.2.1->supported, +H2.22, +H2.22.1, +H2.23, +H2.23.1, +H2.18.4, +H2.20.6, +H2.21.4, +H11.2.2, +H8.3, +H8.3.1, +H7.6, +H7.6.1, +H13, +H13.1, +H13.1.1, +H9.2.3. The 100-seed instrument now drives the tree.

**Status changes:**
- **Refuted:** H2.11.6 (E126), H2.20.4 (E125), H2.20.5 arm (a) (E129), H8.2/H8.2.1/H8.2.2 (E114 null at 100 seeds), and H10.1, which moves from retired to refuted.
- **Supported:** H2.10/H2.10.6, since E128 measured the yardstick at ~1 pp per 32 px epoch, ~0.05 pp per 1% of time, symmetric. H2.11 and H2.11.3 are rewritten: E126 shows the bs-1024 late phases are a real purchase (~0.085 pp per 1%).
- **Narrowed and reopened:** H10's refutation now covers only placement-independent update value. H11 reopens in narrowed form (late fresh full-res samples x updates bind). H11.2 and H11.2.1 are supported by the E121-vs-E126 contrast. A confound ablation is added because E126 also changed the EMA-window samples, the SGD rescale and the Muon path length.
- **Un-retired:** H2.11.5 (bs 768 late), because the premise it was retired on is gone.

**H2 rewritten.** Stale levers are removed. The FLOP-proportional claim is narrowed to where it was measured and handed to a falsifiable FLOP + byte cost-model node. Measured lever rates and a 'funded frontier' node are added: combine sub-yardstick levers with 32 px re-spend.

**H2.18 (depth cuts).** Recomputed with the measured slope (2/3/3 nets only ~-0.7% if re-spent). 3/3/2 is split out as its own test.

**H2.18.3 retired** on search evidence.

**Freeze line.** E125 and E129 are folded in. The 75/80% points are now the key test, and FreezeOut's BN-eval arm is added (search).

**H4 corrected.** The gate tally is now 2 of 7 passes, mean 0.7517, p ≈ 27%. E123's provenance is flagged.

**H4.9 rewritten** as a pre-registered acceptance rule from first principles: official-safety floor 0.7513, at most 3 attempts, and pass probability reported with every banked time.

**H8 restated** as an early-threshold mechanism with falsifiable predictions: a 16 px trim and early bs 2048.

**New Lvl1 N_audit:** 100-seed removal ablations of zero-time components adopted on weak evidence. The lookahead and final-EMA removal tests are given priority. Search lowers the prior that averaging matters under Muon.

**New Muon-C lead** under H7 (search 2609.09676): restricted to the low-res phases and gated on an untimed cost profile.

Open Lvl1s: H2, H8, H9, H11, H12, N_audit.
added I141, I142, I143, I144, I145, I146; dropped none. The tip is the E116 code: 4.262 s with a population mean of 0.7521 (~0.08 pp above the H4.9 floor of 0.7513). The measured yardstick is ~0.05 pp of accuracy per 1% of time (E128).

So the plan is to measure the cheap time levers that have not been tested yet, each on the 100-seed instrument, and then combine every lever that trades below the yardstick with 32 px re-spend (H2.23.1).

**Exploit:**
- **16 px trim, 2.0 → 1.5 epochs (H8.3.1, priority 5):** about -3% time at a predicted ≤0.05 pp loss. The whitening-bias detach and the frozen-sample count stay at fixed positions, so the run measures the trim alone and needs no new graph variants.
- **80% freeze point (H2.20.2, priority 4):** about -1.5% more time than the 85% freeze; this measures the marginal rate.
- **Early bs 2048 with the warmup fixed in steps (H2.11.7, priority 3):** about -1.3% time, and it tests the early-threshold view.

**Smaller or explore:**
- **BN eval mode in the frozen window (H2.20.6):** the same run also does the H2.21.3 measurement, comparing the actual frozen-step saving with its FLOP fraction.
- **Group-3 width 512 (H2.19.2):** a -5% FLOP lever, run only after I139 (the 3/3/2 depth cut) reports.
- **bs 768 in the 28/32 px phases (H2.11.5):** the mirror of E126. It tests whether extra late updates can pay for cuts at better than the 32 px re-spend rate.

Already queued: I134 (translate 4, H12.3.1) and I140 (lookahead removal, H9.2.2), so the queue now holds 8 ideas. I139 (3/3/2) is running. Nothing is dropped, because every queued hypothesis is still open.
